Of course, it depends on the context.  In the case we're discussing, 
my understanding is that the picture of a monkey in a classroom was
labeled "Intuitively Obvious", and that this phrase, at MIT, is the
name of an orientation program for minority students.  If this is
all true, then I think there's a case to be made.  Neither I nor anybody 
else is claiming that *all* monkeys are racist representations of blacks; 
only that *some* can be.

